"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both disclosures address the risk of credit losses driven by macroeconomic disruptions and collateral value declines. MS notes that sudden declines in collateral value can result in significant losses even with over-collateralization, especially if there is a single type of collateral (ms_2024_1A_P018_S004). BAC explicitly lists declines in GDP, property values, and asset price corrections as factors that could decrease collateral value and increase credit losses (bac_2024_1A_P036_S003), and mentions geopolitical events and climate change (bac_2024_1A_P036_S001) alongside economic disruptions.",
