"peer_disclosure_id": "gs_2024_1A_D035",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both MS and GS highlight the risk of losses from sudden declines in collateral value or liquidity, particularly in stressed markets. MS warns that sudden declines in value or liquidity of collateral may result in significant losses, especially where there is a single type of collateral (ms_2024_1A_P018_S004). GS states that declines in asset values used as collateral increase funding costs or decrease position sizes, and that sudden declines in value or liquidity of collateral have resulted in significant losses, especially with single-type collateral (gs_2024_1A_P027_S004, gs_2024_1A_P028_S002).",
